{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And now.</b> Since all this is true — and this is the meaning of 'and now' in every place — He said: since this is true, that I have known his suffering and the affliction of his heart." "<b>Behold, the cry of the children of Israel has come to Me.</b> That I have accepted their prayer, since they called upon Me in truth — not in the manner of וַיְפַתּוּהוּ בְּפִיהֶם (Psalms 78:36)." "<b>And I have also seen the oppression.</b> And given the magnitude of the oppression, it is fitting to punish the oppressors, as in וְקֶצֶף גָּדוֹל אֲנִי קוֹצֵף עַל הַגּוֹיִם הַשַּׁאֲנַנִּים אֲשֶׁר אֲנִי קָצַפְתִּי מְעָט וְהֵם עָזְרוּ לְרָעָה (Zechariah 1:15)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:12.467028800Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}